Sval: forget an overflowed item's hidden mark once it moves back to the row

`OverflowableToolbar` marks an item that overflows with no width as hidden,
so a panel holding only hidden items shows no overflow button. The mark
outlives the item's return to the row, so an item hidden when it first
overflowed, such as the split button before a split, counts as hidden the
next time it overflows while shown, and the overflow button disappears with
the item still in the panel.

